{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01HCZpECAk8oqpJeWc782oM3","type":"tool_result","content":"{\"result\":\"{\\\"answer\\\":\\\"The KIP discussion that covers unregistering a controller’s registration from the metadata log is the KIP-1312 thread, and the final design decision was to reuse the existing controller registration record type rather than introduce a new dedicated record type.  \\\\n\\\\n- 2026-04-03T18:29:54.000000Z - mail:5bf246535561f045598ad4c1: “ KIP-1312: Support unregistering controllers” starts the discussion thread.  \\\\n- 2026-04-03T20:09:24.000000Z - mail:6fb537325fe351ea68514fbf: Kevin Wu notes that the unregister operation will use the same registration record type that is already used for controller registrations.  \\\\n- 2026-04-03T20:37:31.000000Z - mail:dbb9ad0ba90f7a1a862c5d37: Kevin Wu confirms that the `kafka-cluster unregister-controller` command operates on the existing controller registration record, not a new type.  \\\\n\\\\nNo records indicate a decision to create a new dedicated metadata record type.\\\",\\\"error\\\":null,\\\"files\\\":[\\\"mail:5bf246535561f045598ad4c1\\\",\\\"mail:6fb537325fe351ea68514fbf\\\",\\\"mail:dbb9ad0ba90f7a1a862c5d37\\\"],\\\"seconds\\\":120.006,\\\"truncated\\\":false,\\\"turns\\\":22,\\\"usage\\\":{\\\"cache_read_tokens\\\":null,\\\"cache_write_tokens\\\":null,\\\"cost_usd\\\":0.0043275,\\\"input_tokens\\\":158121,\\\"output_tokens\\\":12431}}\"}"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"fdc18493-d463-46de-b2d9-7e690d105f64","uuid":"e58ab0a5-85b7-42c2-a218-f6080fea5d4f","timestamp":"2026-09-28T19:22:46.874Z","tool_use_result":{"content":"{\"result\":\"{\\\"answer\\\":\\\"The KIP discussion that covers unregistering a controller’s registration from the metadata log is the KIP-1312 thread, and the final design decision was to reuse the existing controller registration record type rather than introduce a new dedicated record type.  \\\\n\\\\n- 2026-04-03T18:29:54